        "0": {
          "id": "0",
          "name": "main.py",
          "contents": "pet_name = \"Whiskers\"\nbirth_month = \"October\"\n\n# original code name\ncode_name = pet_name + birth_month\nprint(\"Your original code name is: \" + code_name)\n\n# new & improved code name\ncode_name = pet_name[0:3] + birth_month[0:2]\n\nprint(\"Your improved code name is: \" + code_name)",
          "folderId": "0",
          "active": true
        }
      },
      "folders": {
      },
      "openFiles": [
        "0"
      ]
    },
    "long_instructions": "### Investigate\r\n\r\n1. **Change** the value of `pet_name` to \"Al\" (keep birth_month as \"October\"). Run the program.\r\n2. **Discuss** with your partner: What happened when there weren't 3 letters to grab? Did the program break?\r\n3. **Change** the `birth_month` value to `\"\"` with nothing between the quotes. Run the program.\r\n4. **Discuss** what got added to the code name this time?\r\n5. **Now change** `birth_month` to `\" \"` with one space between the quotes. Run the program.\r\n6. **Discuss** with your partner: Compare this output to Step 3's. What's different, even though both looked empty in the code?\r\n7. **Change** the value of `pet_name` to one that's exactly 3 letters long. Talk with your partner about what you expect to happen — then run it and see."
  },
